      "smallPath": "_m/6/z/8/f/amazon-basin-wp/glow-bug-small.webp"
    },
    {
      "filename": "Early Autumn in the Amazon Basin (MODIS 2026-03-24).jpg",
      "title": "File:Early Autumn in the Amazon Basin (MODIS 2026-03-24).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0d/Early_Autumn_in_the_Amazon_Basin_%28MODIS_2026-03-24%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Early_Autumn_in_the_Amazon_Basin_(MODIS_2026-03-24).jpg",
      "width": 7566,
      "height": 5924,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "Public domain",
      "artist": "MODIS Land Rapid Response Team, NASA GSFC",
      "description": "On March 22, 2026, the Moderate Resolution Imaging Spectroradiometer (MODIS) on NASA’s Terra satellite acquired this true-color image of a nearly cloud-free early autumn day in South America’s Amazon Basin.\nWinding rivers, some tan and some dark, cut through the heart of the deep green Amazon rainforest. As the rivers course through the landscape, they help create a wide variety of habitats, such as marshes or floodplains, each supporting its own array of species. Taken together, the Amazon rainforest and the river system remains the most biologically diverse place on Earth, hosting millions of known species.\nThis image highlights the intricate river system of the Amazon Basin. The Rio Negro flows from the northwest to the southeast and is filled with dark water. The Rio Negro flows into the mud-colored Solimões River (also known as the upper Amazon River) just east of the city of Manaus, where they form the Amazon River. The Amazon itself is also filled with muddy sediment and appears distinctly tan.\n\nHaze covers the western portion of the Amazon Basin visible in this image. Most of these fires are not visible in this portion of the rainforest. According to a wider view available on the NASA Worldview App, most of smoke appears to come from fires in the northwest, especially in Venezuela.",
      "dateCreated": "Taken on 22 March 2026",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "amazon-basin-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "6z8f",
      "mediumPath": "_m/6/z/8/f/amazon-basin-wp/early-autumn-in-the-amazon-bas-medium.webp",
      "smallPath": "_m/6/z/8/f/amazon-basin-wp/early-autumn-in-the-amazon-bas-small.webp"
    },
